# Minimal diffs

Change only the lines the task requires. Extra edits make review harder.

- Do not reformat, rewrap, reindent, or restyle code you are not changing.
- Do not reorder imports, rename symbols, or "clean up" surrounding code unless that is the task.
- Preserve existing quotes, spacing, trailing whitespace, and line endings.
- Do not run a formatter or linter autofix across a whole file. If a tool would rewrite unrelated lines, skip it.
- When editing, match the style already on the lines you touch.

```text
❌ BAD — a one-line logic fix that also rewraps and reindents the function
✅ GOOD — the same fix, with every other line left exactly as it was
```

If a necessary change forces nearby lines to move (for example, adding a parameter), keep that movement as small as possible.
